[2026-03-14T19:24:24.070Z] {"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_014vHkDwcVzkMZkjXMGM41G2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All subtasks completed. Here's a summary of what was built:\n\n**1. TripsTabs** (`src/components/TripsTabs.tsx`) — Three tabs (Upcoming/Past/Cancelled) that filter bookings by status. Upcoming shows pending/confirmed with check_in >= today, Past shows completed, Cancelled shows cancelled. Each tab has empty state messages with a \"Browse properties\" link on the Upcoming empty state.\n\n**2. TripCard** (`src/components/TripCard.tsx`) — Displays property image (or placeholder), title, city, date range, status badge with color-coded styling (pending=yellow, confirmed=green, cancelled=red, completed=blue), total price, Cancel button for pending/confirmed bookings, Write Review button for completed bookings without a review, and \"Reviewed ✓\" badge for already-reviewed bookings. Clicking the card navigates to the property detail page.\n\n**3. CancelBookingDialog** (`src/components/CancelBookingDialog.tsx`) — Modal confirmation dialog showing property name and dates, with \"Keep Booking\" and \"Yes, Cancel\" buttons. Clicking the overlay dismisses the dialog.\n\n**4. MyTrips page** (`src/pages/MyTrips.tsx`) — Requires login (redirects to `/login`), fetches user bookings via Redux, renders TripsTabs and manages the CancelBookingDialog state.\n\n**Supporting changes:**\n- Updated `bookingsSlice.ts` with `fetchUserBookings` and `cancelBooking` async thunks\n- Updated `bookings.ts` API to include `has_review` field via subquery on reviews table\n- Added `/trips` route to `App.tsx`\n\n`npm run check` passes.\n\n<DONE>"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":369,"cache_read_input_tokens":55675,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":369,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo"